      <h2 id="where-collagen-fits">Where a collagen shot fits, and where it does not</h2>
      <p>It does not fit at the diagnostic stage at all, and our own label is the clearest way to show why.</p>
      <p>Collabloom contains 8,000mg of Japanese hydrolysed marine collagen per 30ml shot, with 1.5mg zinc and 45mcg biotin among its 17 actives. It contains no iron, no vitamin D and no vitamin B12. The two deficiencies most often found in people who are shedding are therefore two things this product cannot correct, and the zinc and biotin in it are co-factor amounts rather than the doctor-directed doses used to correct a measured deficiency.</p>
      <p>What a collagen shot plausibly supports is dietary protein intake and skin quality, which is where the trial evidence sits, and which <a href="/pages/collagen-for-nails">collagen for nails</a> and <a href="/pages/collagen-side-effects">collagen side effects</a> set out dose by dose. Hair fall with a medical or nutritional cause needs that cause found and treated. Get the tests, then decide what, if anything, is worth buying.</p>

